    vec" optimization, in which common cases can fit on a pre-allocated stack buffer, but rare cases
    need dynamic heap allocation. The previous design had a few problems:There was no way to specify the alignment of the buffer.It was generic over the size of the buffer.Now, the buffer is provided as an argument, like most other std APIs that need a buffer. stack ((
    (std.heap.StackFallbackAllocator()),
